From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dwmapi, uxtheme, winex11: Aero glass frames, live thumbnails and Aero Peek

Purpose: with Aero (0152), Windows 7's window frames, the taskbar's window
thumbnails and Aero Peek as under the desktop window manager.
Windows 7 behavior: the DWM draws every framed window's borders and caption
as glass, with the DWMWindow atlas's caption buttons (one group against the
top of the frame, as high as SM_CYSIZE less one, each as wide as its image
without its glow) and a black title with a white glow; the menu bar and the
window's scroll bars stay opaque. DwmExtendFrameIntoClientArea takes the
glass into the client area (all of it with negative margins). Pointing at a
taskbar button, explorer calls DwmpRegisterThumbnail (ordinal 124:
destination, source, NULL, 1, &thumbnail, as logged from it), sizes it with
DwmQueryThumbnailSourceSize and places it with DwmUpdateThumbnailProperties
(RECTDESTINATION | OPACITY, the client area only, never VISIBLE: a
thumbnail is visible from the start); the DWM draws the source window live.
Pointing at a thumbnail, it calls DwmpActivateLivePreview (113: peek,
window, topmost, type) and the other windows become transparent.
Wine before: frames were Windows 7 Basic's images; DwmExtendFrameIntoClientArea,
DwmRegisterThumbnail, DwmUpdateThumbnailProperties and DwmUnregisterThumbnail
were stubs, DwmQueryThumbnailSourceSize missing, DwmpRegisterThumbnail failed
and DwmpActivateLivePreview did nothing. DwmIsCompositionEnabled was
Windows 10's answer (TRUE) in the Windows 7 session's other programs.
Change: in a Windows 7 session, DwmIsCompositionEnabled gives
WIN4WINE_AERO in every program. uxtheme draws a frame with Aero as glass:
in a buffered paint (alpha 0) with dark and light edges, the atlas's
buttons and glyphs (decoded with WIC from the theme file's stream), and the
title composited with a glow; it copies only the borders and the caption,
says how far the glass goes ("__win4wine_glass_frame") and calls
DwmExtendFrameIntoClientArea, which makes the window glass and keeps its
margins. winex11 keeps the alpha of a glass frame's window outside the
part that stays opaque (client area and menu bar, less the margins), which
it updates when the surface is kept. Thumbnails are a table in dwmapi, which
winex11 (same process) reads from the destination's property and draws at
each flush of a glass destination: each source's X window (its pixmap,
kept by the session's Composite redirection) scaled with a box filter; a
thread redraws visible thumbnails four times a second. Aero Peek makes the
other top-level windows transparent with _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY, through a
new winex11 escape on the display DC, and puts them back at its end.
Scope: WIN4WINE_AERO with WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7; thumbnails and Peek are
64-bit (Windows 7's taskbar), the 32-bit forms of 113 and 124 stay stubs.
